/* Intro */
The loud crunch of your sneakers walking over the gravel in the driveway gives way to a soft scuff as you walk into the grass and weeds. <span style="color:Yellow">You don’t know where you’re headed, and you certainly don’t have a plan, which is exactly how an exploration should start.</span> Trekking past the red barn, you leave the domestic lawn and enter the wild field beyond where scents of dry grass and wild clover lead you forward. <br>
<br>
The further you walk, the more the world quietens. Eventually the main sounds are the rhythmic thrum of cicada, and a distant bleating of an animal you don’t see. Towards the edge of the field, you come across a wooden fence. It is well weathered as the wood is silvered by years of rain and sunlight. Walking parallel to the fence, you trail your hand over the wooden railing, your fingers tracing over the rough, sun-warmed wood. <br>
<br>
On the other side a field of grain fills your vision. Sun-baked golden stalks stand up, erect in rows, swaying slightly in a slow-motion dance. On the horizon, a heavy shiver starts amongst the stalks as the wind rolls towards you. You see the wake of the wind before it reaches you as a pale silvery ripple on the sea of grain. A faint hiss from the stalks bowing their heads accompanies the wind as it passes over you. <span style="color:LightGreen">Closing your eyes, you feel the cool air tickle your skin. Smells of cereal and dirt fill your nostrils as you breathe in deeply.</span> <br>

